  "step_3": "The decision reason requires attention to the maximum loss and a weighting of losses as more important than gains. However, the individual does not refer to losses at all; instead, the deliberation centers on gains and probabilities of winning. Furthermore, since both lotteries have identical maximum losses (0 Euros), even if the individual had considered losses, there would be no distinction between the lotteries on that basis. The information considered by the individual (probabilities and gains) does not align with the information required by the decision reason (maximum losses). The justification based on higher gains in B contradicts the reason’s principle of prioritizing losses over gains. Therefore, there is no evidence that the decision reason was used in the deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
